%N A401619 Largest integer k such that, for every positive integer m, there exists a k-element subset of {1, ..., n} with no subset summing to m.
%C A401619 This is f(n) in Erdős Problem 771.
%H A401619 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/771">Erdős Problem 771</a>, Erdős Problems.
%F A401619 a(n-1) <= a(n) <= a(n-1) + 1 for n >= 2.
